{"timestamp":"2026-05-23T12:20:20.294Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"tool_search_output","call_id":"call_Se6lmV74ZaOtLsmUugmB8boL","status":"completed","execution":"client","tools":[{"type":"namespace","name":"mcp__xcodebuildmcp__","description":"XcodeBuildMCP provides comprehensive tooling for Apple platform development (iOS, macOS, watchOS, tvOS, visionOS).\n\nPrefer XcodeBuildMCP tools over shell commands for Apple platform tasks when available.\n\nCapabilities:\n- Session defaults: Configure project, scheme, simulator, and device defaults to avoid repetitive parameters\n- Project discovery: Find Xcode projects/workspaces, list schemes, inspect build settings\n- Simulator workflows: Build, run, test, install, and launch apps on iOS simulators; manage simulator state (boot, erase, location, appearance)\n- Device workflows: Build, test, install, and launch apps on physical devices with code signing\n- macOS workflows: Build, run, and test macOS applications\n- Log capture: Stream and capture logs from simulators and devices\n- LLDB debugging: Attach debugger, set breakpoints, inspect stack traces and variables, execute LLDB commands\n- UI automation: Capture screenshots, inspect view hierarchy with coordinates, perform taps/swipes/gestures, type text, press hardware buttons\n- SwiftPM: Build, run, test, and manage Swift Package Manager projects\n- Project scaffolding: Generate new iOS/macOS project templates\n\nOnly simulator workflow tools are enabled by default. If capabilities like device, macOS, debugging, or UI automation are not available, the user must configure XcodeBuildMCP to enable them. See https://xcodebuildmcp.com/docs/configuration for workflow configuration.\n\nSimulator run flow:\n- Before your first build, run, or test call in a session, you MUST call session_show_defaults to verify the active project/workspace, scheme, and simulator. Do not assume defaults are configured. Only skip this if you have already called session_show_defaults earlier in the current session.\n- If session_show_defaults confirms project/workspace + scheme + simulator are set, call build_run_sim immediately (often with empty arguments).\n- Use discover_projs only when session_show_defaults shows project/workspace is missing or wrong.\n- Never call discover_projs speculatively or in parallel with session_show_defaults.\n- Do not call boot_sim or open_sim as prerequisites for build_run_sim; build_run_sim boots and opens Simulator as needed.","tools":[{"type":"function","name":"screenshot","description":"Capture screenshot. This tool is part of plugin `Build iOS Apps`.","strict":false,"defer_loading":true,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"returnFormat":{"type":"string","description":"Return image path or base64 data (path|base64)","enum":["path","base64"]}}}},{"type":"function","name":"build_run_sim","description":"Build, install, and launch on iOS Simulator; boots simulator and attempts to open Simulator.app as needed. Runtime logs are captured automatically and the log file path is included in the response. Preferred single-step run tool when defaults are set. This tool is part of plugin `Build iOS Apps`.","strict":false,"defer_loading":true,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"extraArgs":{"type":"array","description":"Additional xcodebuild/build-settings arguments (not app launch arguments)","items":{"type":"string"}},"launchArgs":{"type":"array","description":"Arguments passed to the launched app process on simulator runtime","items":{"type":"string"}}}}},{"type":"function","name":"launch_app_sim","description":"Launch app on simulator. Runtime logs are captured automatically and the log file path is included in the response. This tool is part of plugin `Build iOS Apps`.","strict":false,"defer_loading":true,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"env":{"type":"object","description":"Environment variables to pass to the launched app (SIMCTL_CHILD_ prefix added automatically)","properties":{},"additionalProperties":{"type":"string"}},"launchArgs":{"type":"array","description":"Arguments passed to the launched app process on simulator runtime","items":{"type":"string"}}}}},{"type":"function","name":"open_sim","description":"Open Simulator.app for visibility/manual workflows. Not required before simulator build-and-run (build_run_sim). This tool is part of plugin `Build iOS Apps`.","strict":false,"defer_loading":true,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"type":"function","name":"stop_app_sim","description":"Stop sim app. This tool is part of plugin `Build iOS Apps`.","strict":false,"defer_loading":true,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"type":"function","name":"install_app_sim","description":"Install app on sim. This tool is part of plugin `Build iOS Apps`.","strict":false,"defer_loading":true,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"appPath":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the .app bundle to install"}},"required":["appPath"]}},{"type":"function","name":"get_app_bundle_id","description":"Extract bundle id from .app. This tool is part of plugin `Build iOS Apps`.","strict":false,"defer_loading":true,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"appPath":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the .app bundle"}},"required":["appPath"]}},{"type":"function","name":"get_sim_app_path","description":"Get sim built app path. This tool is part of plugin `Build iOS Apps`.","strict":false,"defer_loading":true,"parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"platform":{"type":"string","enum":["iOS Simulator","watchOS Simulator","tvOS Simulator","visionOS Simulator"]}},"required":["platform"]}}]}]}}
